GECToR grammatical error correction model
Weights: gotutiyan/gector-roberta-base-5k, revision
adaac6fb919431fb5a038b1e449055ae638613a4, https://huggingface.co/gotutiyan/gector-roberta-base-5k
Copyright gotutiyan. Its model card states: "Only non-commercial purposes".
Parzr is free software distributed without charge and uses these weights only
on that basis; anyone who redistributes or sells a build must check that
condition for themselves. The model implements GECToR: Omelianchuk, Atrasevych,
Chernodub, Skurzhanskyi, "GECToR: Grammatical Error Correction: Tag, Not
Rewrite" (BEA 2020), a Grammarly project. Parzr downloads a Core ML conversion
(static 80 token input, fp16 or int8 weight-only) made by scripts/convert-gector.py;
revisions, versions and SHA-256 hashes are in the pack's gector/manifest.json.
roberta-base: Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc. and its affiliates (fairseq). MIT license.
https://huggingface.co/roberta-base, https://github.com/facebookresearch/fairseq
Its byte level BPE vocabulary (vocab.json, merges.txt) ships with the model. The full
MIT license text ships as resources/ThirdParty/RoBERTa-fairseq-MIT-LICENSE.txt (in the
app: Resources/ThirdParty/RoBERTa-fairseq-MIT-LICENSE.txt).
Output label vocabulary and verb form vocabulary (verb-form-vocab.txt):
grammarly/gector, commit 4ad259f25c6bb408a99788d468cd8958845e647e,
https://github.com/grammarly/gector. Copyright Grammarly, Inc. Apache License 2.0
(resources/ThirdParty/GECToR-Grammarly-Apache-2.0.txt).
The model runs entirely on the device; nothing is sent.

distilroberta-base (the word-choice check while typing, optional "slips" pack, downloaded while Slip check is on, the default)
Weights: distilbert/distilroberta-base, revision
fb53ab8802853c8e4fbdbcd0529f21fc6f459b2b, https://huggingface.co/distilbert/distilroberta-base
Copyright Hugging Face. Apache License 2.0. Distilled from roberta-base (Facebook
AI Research, MIT license); its byte level BPE vocabulary (vocab.json, merges.txt)
ships with the model. Parzr downloads a Core ML conversion (int8 weight-only, the
masked-language-model head scored at one position per row) made by
scripts/convert-slips.py; revisions, versions and SHA-256 hashes are in the pack's
slips/manifest.json. The model runs entirely on the device; nothing is sent.

Tone check model (the optional "tone" pack, downloaded while Tone check is on, the default)
Fine-tuned from sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2, revision
1110a243fdf4706b3f48f1d95db1a4f5529b4d41, https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
(based on microsoft/MiniLM-L6-H384-uncased). Apache License 2.0. Its BERT uncased
WordPiece vocabulary (vocab.txt) ships with the model, unchanged. The fine-tuned
network is converted to Core ML with 8-bit weights by scripts/tone-check.
Training data (pack version 2): lines written for Parzr (synthetic), the Stanford
Politeness Corpus (Danescu-Niculescu-Mizil et al., 2013, CC BY 4.0) and the Civil
Comments validation shard (google/civil_comments, CC0). No private writing was used,
and no data under use-restricted (RAIL) licenses.
The model runs entirely on the device; nothing is sent.

The engine tokenizes sentences for the model as spaCy 3.8 does. Its English tokenizer rules
(engine/rules/gec-tokenizer.json: prefix, suffix and infix patterns and the special-case table)
are exported from spaCy, Copyright ExplosionAI GmbH, spaCy GmbH and Matthew Honnibal. MIT license.
https://github.com/explosion/spaCy. The full license text ships as resources/ThirdParty/spaCy-MIT-LICENSE.txt
(in the app: Resources/ThirdParty/spaCy-MIT-LICENSE.txt).

Production edit alignment uses similar 3.2.0 (Apache-2.0,
resources/ThirdParty/similar-3.2.0/LICENSE) and unicode-segmentation 1.13.3
(MIT/Apache-2.0, resources/ThirdParty/unicode-segmentation-1.13.3).
The rule and frequency credits above cover production grammar/spelling passes
and research source. Production combines those passes with the bundled model.

